{
  "chapter": "security/sandboxing",
  "tier": "drill",
  "notes": [
    "The sandbox holds no credentials. It reaches a broker over one socket and asks for an",
    "operation, never for a secret — and there is no request kind that returns one, because",
    "it was never implemented.",
    "The broker runs the same authorization the tool dispatcher runs. Generated code cannot",
    "reach anything the model could not have called directly, or you have built a second,",
    "unreviewed tool interface that voids the least-privilege work.",
    "Egress is deny by default with an allowlist. The package registry is denied at runtime,",
    "because installing inside a live sandbox is third-party code execution mid-run.",
    "A denied connection to an unexpected host is the highest-signal detection available",
    "here, so egress and secret denials alert. An ordinary authorization refusal does not.",
    "Sandbox output becomes tool results, which become prompt text, so it is truncated at",
    "the boundary rather than after it has entered the window."
  ],
  "policy": {
    "egressAllow": ["broker.internal", "api.provider.example"],
    "maxOutputBytes": 32768,
    "catalogue": {
      "get_order": { "class": 1 },
      "search_policies": { "class": 1 },
      "run_sql": { "class": 3 },
      "issue_credit": { "class": 4 }
    }
  },
  "scope": { "maxClass": 3, "orderId": "4921", "capCents": 100000 },
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "an-operation-inside-the-scope-is-served",
